<category><pattern>WHAT IS ETHEREUM</pattern><template>Ethereum is a decentralized blockchain that provides smart contract functionality.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHO CONCEIVED ETHEREUM AND WHEN WAS IT CREATED</pattern><template>It was conceived in 2013 by programmer Vitalik Buterin.</template></category>
<category><pattern>CAN ANYONE DEPLOY APPLICATIONS ON ETHEREUM AND CAN THEY USE THEM</pattern><template>Yes, anyone can deploy decentralized applications onto Ethereum, and then use them.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHAT TYPE OF ASSETS OR TOKENS CAN USERS CREATE ON ETHEREUM</pattern><template>Users can create fungible assets such as tokens (e.g., ERC-20).</template></category>
<category><pattern>IS ETHEREUM OPEN TO ALL PARTICIPANTS</pattern><template>Ethereum allows anyone to deploy and use applications, making it accessible to a broad audience.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHAT IS THE PURPOSE OF SMART CONTRACTS ON ETHEREUM</pattern><template>Smart contracts enable automated execution of agreements directly on the blockchain without intermediaries.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHEN WAS ETHEREUM FIRST INTRODUCED CONCEIVED</pattern><template>Ethereum was conceived in 2013.</template></category>
<category><pattern>DOES ETHEREUM SUPPORT DECENTRALIZED APPLICATIONS DAPPS</pattern><template>Yes, it allows anyone to deploy and use decentralized applications on its network.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHAT IS THE EQUATION OF THE ELLIPTIC CURVE FOR SECP256K1</pattern><template>The curve is defined by y^2 = x^3 + 7 over the real numbers, but its actual graph uses points in the finite field Z_p.</template></category>
<category><pattern>OVER WHICH NUMBER SYSTEM IS SECP256K1 ACTUALLY DEFINED</pattern><template>It is defined over the field Z_p (a large prime field).</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHY DOES THE GRAPH OF THIS CURVE LOOK LIKE RANDOM SCATTERED POINTS</pattern><template>Because secp256k1&#x27;s graph uses elements from a finite field, not real numbers; thus its discrete points appear as scattered points rather than a smooth curve.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHAT FIELD IS SECP256K1 DEFINED OVER</pattern><template>It is defined over the finite field Z/p (where p is a large prime).</template></category>
<category><pattern>IS THERE ANY MENTION OF DATES OR FOUNDING YEAR FOR SECP256K1 IN THIS REPORT</pattern><template>No specific date is given; the focus is on its mathematical definition and graph appearance.</template></category>
<category><pattern>HOW DOES THE REAL NUMBER VERSION DIFFER FROM THE ACTUAL CURVE USED IN PRACTICE</pattern><template>The real-number equation y^2 = x^3 + 7 would produce a smooth cubic, but over Z_p it becomes discrete points that look random.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHO STARTED THE GEMINI PROTOCOL</pattern><template>It was started in June 2019 by a pseudonymous person known as Solderpunk.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHEN DID THE USENET NEWSGROUP COMP INFOSYSTEMS GEMINI GET CREATED</pattern><template>October 2021, which is noted as the first new newsgroup in the Big Eight hierarchy in eight years.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHAT IS GEMINI S PURPOSE RELATIVE TO GOPHER AND HTTP</pattern><template>Gemini is not intended to replace Gopher or HTTP but is designed to co-exist with them.</template></category>
<category><pattern>IS GEMINI STANDARDIZED BY THE IETF</pattern><template>No, it has not yet been submitted to the IETF organization for standardization.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHAT FORMAT DOES GEMINI USE FOR ITS DOCUMENTS</pattern><template>It uses a special document format called &#x27;gemtext&#x27; which allows linking to other documents and is analogous to HTML for HTTP.</template></category>
<category><pattern>HOW SHOULD CONNECTIONS IN THE GEMINI PROTOCOL BE SECURED</pattern><template>Gemini mandates the use of TLS (Transport Layer Security) with privacy-related features and TOFU verification being strongly suggested.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHAT PORT DOES A GEMINI SERVER LISTEN ON</pattern><template>A Gemini server should listen on TCP port 1965.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHAT IS LLAMA CPP</pattern><template>llama.cpp is an open-source software library that performs inference on various large language models such as Meta&#x27;s Llama model.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHO CREATED A SIMILAR LIBRARY BEFORE LLAMA CPP</pattern><template>Gerganov worked on whisper.cpp, which implemented Whisper, a speech-to-text model by OpenAI, prior to llama.cpp.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHERE CAN YOU DOWNLOAD AND RUN COMPATIBLE GGUF MODELS FOR LLAMA CPP</pattern><template>You can download and run them directly from the Hugging Face Hub via llama.cpp.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHEN DID PFSENSE ADD WIREGUARD SUPPORT</pattern><template>In February 2021, pfSense CE 2.5.0 and pfSense Plus 21.02 added support for a kernel WireGuard implementation.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHY WAS WIREGUARD SUPPORT TEMPORARILY REMOVED IN MARCH 2021</pattern><template>Support for WireGuard was temporarily removed after implementation issues were discovered by WireGuard founder Jason Donenfeld.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHEN DID PFSENSE RE INCLUDE WIREGUARD</pattern><template>The July 2021 release of pfSense CE 2.5.2 version re-included WireGuard.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHAT IS BITCOIN</pattern><template>Bitcoin is the first decentralized cryptocurrency.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHO INVENTED BITCOIN</pattern><template>Bitcoin was invented in 2008 when an unknown person published a white paper under the pseudonym of Satoshi Nakamoto.</template></category>
<category><pattern>WHEN WAS THE BITCOIN GENESIS BLOCK MINED</pattern><template>On 3 January 2009, Satoshi Nakamoto mined the genesis block of bitcoin (block number 0), which had a reward of 50 bitcoins.</template></category>
